# Explicit public development objectives

Twelve new public examples define concrete objectives for the original XML,
OAuth and Click development prefixes. They use the retained public titles and
actual prefix-source APIs. No hidden test or reference patch was inspected, and
no model or scorer was called. These are **author-written development contracts**;
they are not recovered historical issue bodies or new independent families.
The separately retained Pyparsing public-report reproduction supplies the fourth
original development objective.

| Unchanged prefix | Examples conforming | Observation |
|---|---:|---|
| XML, `75a17701` | 2/4 | Namespace declarations move from an attribute-free declaring element to its child in both authored namespace cases. |
| OAuth, `cf3cf407` | 1/4 | Authorization-only, explicit response-type and combined Server metadata raise the same AttributeError; token-only metadata returns successfully. |
| Click, `02046e7a` | 2/4 | Both hidden-choice help cases still enumerate choices; visible-choice and explicit-metavar controls pass. |

The three fresh subprocesses complete within their frozen 60-second bounds.
Full inventories retain 16, 199 and 145 source entries, respectively. Actual
package imports come from those prefixes. The independent read-only audit passes
545 checks, reconstructing all twelve predicates, source hashes/modes, imported
module hashes and process records. It executes no additional target code.

`run-v1` is retained as an unsuccessful qualification: the probe omitted the
required `default_token_type` argument for three OAuth constructors. Those three
TypeErrors are harness errors, not target defects. The revised runner uses a
real BearerToken, includes all required combined-server endpoint claims, and
corrects the combined Server's expected public response types to include `none`.
`run-v2` freezes the corrected examples before execution and has no setup errors.
Each run retains its exact runner bytes and observations.

`objectives-v1.json` binds the new objective text, allowed repair surface, examples,
public API sources and qualification inputs. An independently admitted scorer
still governs whole-task acceptance. A complete caller, source/configuration
events, lifecycle reuse, warm priming and the original comparison matrix remain
required. The observed 5/12 conformity total is an example result, not a repair
success estimate or system quality metric. Python and third-party runtime
dependencies were not frozen as a deployable environment by this small probe.
